# Naming and Single-Responsibility Audit: Independent Findings, Verdicts
File: openOODA/audits/naming/devin_verdicts.oot

Provenance: converted from `openOODA/audits/naming-audit-devin.md` (283 lines). Part 2 of 2.

## 4. Category 3 — Ambiguous, Redundant & Colliding Names

### 4.1 Duplicate embedding (same name, two canonical hosts) — **the sharpest defect**

| Persona/repo | Host 1 | Host 2 | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| `oodns-cloud` | `oomesh` (RFC-correct) | `oogateway` | DNS embedded in *both* L6 edge hosts |
| `ooqueue` | `oodb-dist` | `oosched-cloud` | Queue lives in DB *and* scheduler |
| `ooclip` | `oofiles` | `ooportal` | Clipboard in file manager *and* portal |
| `ooshot` | `oofiles` | `ooportal` | Screenshot in both |
| `ootaskmgr` | `oofiles` | `oocockpit` | …and oocockpit itself is absorbed into oopanel |
| `ooarchitect` | `oogovern` | `oooda-engine` (`persona/architect.oo`) | Architect in two L7 hosts |
| `oohealthd` | `ooinit` (`healthd/` subtree) | standalone repo still ships | Dual existence, not marked absorbed |

These are not personas-by-design (a persona is a token inside ONE binary); they are **copied subtrees in two repos**, i.e.,
forked sources of truth that will drift.

### 4.2 Inverted absorptions (code contradicts RFC)

Table columns: Pair | RFC 0012 says | Code does
- `oomail`/`oochat` | `oomail` canonical; `oochat` dropped | `oomail` marked **Absorbed → into `oochat`**
- `ooreviewer`/`oocoder` | `oocoder` canonical; `ooreviewer` dropped | `ooreviewer` contains `oocoder/` (30 pages)
- `oodeploy`/`oobuild-fleet` | `oodeploy` absorbs `oobuild-fleet` | both directions exist: `oodeploy`⊃fleet+infer+sched **and**
  `oobuild-fleet`⊃`oodeploy/` (32 pages)
- `ooagent-hud`/`oocockpit` | `ooagent-hud` canonical; `oocockpit` dropped | `oocockpit` embeds `ooagent-hud` (while cockpit
  itself → `oopanel`)
- `oonotes`/`oopdf` | canonical standalone | also personas inside `oodocs` (dual existence)

### 4.3 Redundant/overlapping families (intra-layer)

- **Diffs (11)**: `oodiff, oodiff3, oocmp, oocomm, oosdiff, oowdiff, oobindiff, oogitdiff, oosemantcdiff, ooschemadiff,
   oostructureddiff, ooastdiff` — RFC folds 6 into `oodiff`; the *diff suffix zoo* remains 4 overlapping "semantic" differ
  names.
- **Digests (8)**: `oohash, oob3sum, oochecksum, oocrc32, oosha256, oosha512, oomd5` (+`oocksum` persona token). `oochecksum` vs
  `oohash` unmapped overlap.
- **Arch/compress (9)**: `ooarchive, ootar, oo7z, oocpio, oounzip, oogzip, oobzip2, ooxz, oozstd` (+ghost `oozip`).
- **Net admin (~20)**: `oocurl/oowget/oowget2/oofetch`, `oonetcat/oosock/ooss/oonetstat`, `ooip/ooifconfig/ooarp/ooroute`,
  `ooiptables/oonftables/oofirewall`, `ooping/oomtr/ootraceroute`, `oodig/oohost/oonslookup/oodns/oowhois`,
  `ooscp/oosftp/oossh/ootunnel/oorproxy`. Three firewalls, four DNS lookups, three iface tools.
- **Sandbox/security (~18)**:
  `oocap/oolandlock/ooseccomp/ooapparmor/oochroot/oocgroup(+v2)/ooguard/oosandbox/oonaa/oonegatrust/oopolicy/ootaint` vs
  `OS/oorealm` vs `tools/ooaudit/ooattest/ooprovenance`.
- **Sign/crypto (~10)**: `oosign/ooverify/oocert/ookeygen/oovault/ootoken/oossl/ootls/oossh/oonegatrust` — `oossl`≈`ootls` (same
  upstream).
- **TUI widgets (~19)**:
  `ooansi/oocolor/oorgb/oohsl/oogradient/oote/oopreset/ooglyph/oofigure/ooborder/ootable/oobanner/oosparkline/oobar/oopr
  ogress/oospinner/oodialog/oomenubar/ooprompt` — 3 progress bars (`oobar/ooprogress/oosparkline`), 4 color tools.
- **Monitoring (~16)**: `oowatch/ooswatch/oomonitor/ootop` (4 watchers!), `ooiostat/oompstat/oovmstat/oosensors`,
  `oohwinfo/oolshw/oolspci/oolsusb/oocpuinfo`, `oomeminfo/oofree`, `oodf/oodu`, `oodmesg/oojournal`.
- **Pagers/viewers (7)**: `ooless/oomore/oocat/oohex/ooxxd/oobiew` + `DE/ooview` + `apps/oopdf`.
- **Agents overlap**: `oorouter`≈`ooherdr` (both score capability-masked agents by load and dispatch); `ooredteam`≈`oofalsify`
  (both adversarial boundary generators); `ooarchitect`≈`oogovern`≈`oorelease` (all audit VERSION/ooda.pkg/LICENSE/ci.yml);
  `ooplanner`≈`oooda-engine` (both import-graph→build-order).
- **Scheduler collisions across layers**: `tools/{ooat,oobatch,oocron,ooworker}` vs `cloud/oosched-cloud` vs
  `kernel/ookernel-sched` — "sched" means 3 unrelated things.
- **`oosession`/`ooscreen`/`ootmux`/`oologinctl`/`ooworker`** — session/mux/process cluster blurs layers.

### 4.4 Missing coverage (naming gaps)

No repos for core tools the fleet otherwise duplicates: `oodate`, `oodd`, `ooecho`, `oocal`, `ooed`, `oowhich` (persona-only),
`ootee` (name squatted by `oote`), `oozip`. `ooflash`'s `rawio.oo` wraps host `dd` because **no `oodd` exists** — an ironic gap
for a stack that otherwise reimplements everything.

