- `OS/oopowerd` | `OS/oodevd` | `oodevd/power/` subtree
- `OS/oosvc-mgr` | `OS/ooinit` | `ooinit/svcmgr/` subtree
- `OS/oofs-ext4`, `oofs-tmp` | `OS/oovfs` | `oovfs/{ext4,tmp}/` subtrees
- `cloud/{oocdn}` | `oogateway` | embedded; **but also dup'd inside `oomesh`? no — `oodns-cloud` is the dup; oocdn only in
  gateway**
- `cloud/{oobuild-fleet,ooinfer-grid,oosched-cloud}` | `oodeploy` | subtrees in `oodeploy/` — *but see F1/F2 reverse+dup
  embeddings*
- `cloud/{oostore-cas,ooregistry-cloud}` | `oostore` | subtrees in `oostore/`
- `cloud/{oodns-cloud,oorelay}` | `oomesh` | subtrees in `oomesh/` — `oodns-cloud` is **dup'd in `oogateway`** (resolve first)
- `cloud/{ooconsent}` | `ooidentity` | subtree in `ooidentity/` (RFC-silent; sensible fill)
- `cloud/{ooqueue}` | `oodb-dist` | subtree in `oodb-dist/` — **also in `oosched-cloud`** (resolve F2)
- `DE/{oowm,oowall}` | `oocomp` | `oocomp/core/persona/{oowm,oowall}/`
- `DE/{ooview,ooedit,ooclip,ooshot,ootaskmgr}` | `oofiles` | `oofiles/core/persona/*` — `ooclip`/`ooshot`/`ootaskmgr` **dup'd**
  (resolve F2)
- `DE/{oocockpit,oolaunch,ooshelf,ootoast}` | `oopanel` | `oopanel/core/persona/*`
- `agents/{ooarchitect,oorelease}` | `oogovern` | subtrees present
- `agents/{ooredteam}` | `oofalsify` | subtree present
- `agents/{ooeval,ooevolve}` | `ooconsensus` | subtrees present
- `agents/{ooplanner,ooarchitect}` | `oooda-engine` | `persona/{planner,architect}.oo` — `ooarchitect` **dup'd** with oogovern
- `kernel`: per persona tables | see below | registry-level personas (`absorbed_set.oo`), no full subtrees — **not** ready until
  domain impls are actually ported

**NOT ready to archive:** the 104 skeleton stubs in tools (they are *unimplemented*, not *absorbed* — backlog work, keep on the
backlog board); `oonotes`/`oopdf`/`oomail`/`oohealthd`/`oolock`/`ooagent-hud`/`oodeploy`-in-fleet until duplicate-embedding and
RFC-inversion verdicts are made; anything whose "absorption" is only a `persona/absorbed_set.oo` registry entry with no ported
domain logic (kernel set, parts of OS).

### 5.2 KEEP (canonical hosts, correctly named)

`core`: all 9 (`cli ooda oodac oodar opm lsp mcp std tui`) — clean N-binary roles per §1.14.
`tools`: ~64-canonical set is right in shape:
`oosh, oogrep, oofind, oojq, oocurl, oodiff, oob3sum, ootar/ooarchive, oosh(via oosh personas), oote? (rename), ootop,
 ools, oocat, ooless, oosort, oosed, ooawk…` plus `oowatch` (keep — pick over `ooswatch`).
`OS`: `ooinit, oovfs, oonetd, oosysbus, oohealthd(or fold into ooinit as it already is), ooimage, ooaid` (+ `oosession`→rename
`ooauthd`).
`DE`: `oocomp, oofiles, oopanel, ooportal, ooterm, oosettings, oolock, oobazaar, ooagent-hud` — matches RFC's 9 (implementation
confirms).
`apps`: `oobrowser, oostudio, oodocs→rename, oocanvas, oomedia, oodaw, oopdf?, oomail?, oopass, oovm-ui, ooflash` (+`oochat` vs
`oomail` decision).
`cloud`: `oomesh, oostore, oodeploy, oogateway, ooidentity, oodb-dist, ootelemetry, oobilling` (+`ooqueue` either canonical or
committed to `oodb-dist`).
`agents`: `oooda-engine, ooherdr, ooquota, oofalsify, ooconsensus, oocoder, oomemory, oogovern` (+resolve `ooreviewer`/`oocoder`
inversion, `oorouter` vs `ooherdr` overlap).

### 5.3 RENAME candidates

- `oodocs` → **`oooffice`** (it is the office suite; "docs" undersells sheet+deck+pdf; aligns with RFC).
- `oosession`(+`policy/`) → **`ooauthd`** (RFC name; session+policy is the auth daemon).
- `ookernel-boot` → **`ooboot`**; `ookernel-hal-{x86,arm64,riscv}` → **`oohal`** (one repo, arch personas); `oodrv-{nvme…}` → **
  `oodrv-storage`**; `oodrv-{display-gop,usb-hid…}` → **`oodrv-io`**; `oodrv-{virtio,pci?}` → **`oodrv-virt`** — i.e., implement
  the RFC's L1 naming instead of today's arbitrary pairwise absorbs.
- `oosqllite` → `oosqlite` (or fold into `ooquery`/db persona).
- `oote` → keep function, consider `ootheme` (releases the `tee` namespace); or accept squatting + add `ootee`/`tee` persona
  under `oocat`.
- `oobiew` → `oohexview`? (or persona under `oohex`/`ooxxd`); at minimum disambiguate from `DE/ooview`.
- `ooboundary`/`oobound` → merge to one name (`oobound`) with `egress` persona.
- `openOODA-tools.github.io` — GitHub-forced name; document it as non-product in `northstar` to fix the 257-vs-258 count drift.

### 5.4 SPLIT candidates

- **`oodocs`**: if `oochat` precedent (fat multi-persona app binary) is unloved, split `oosheet`/`oodeck` impls back out — but
  the cleaner verdict is *rename, don't split*.
- **`oofiles`**: split `ootaskmgr`+`ooedit` personas out of the file manager OR move `ooclip`/`ooshot` to `ooportal` permanently
  (dedupe F2) and let `oofiles` keep `ooview`/`ooedit` as preview/open-with personas.
- **`oocat`**: split pager half into `ooless` (or keep as `oocat view` subcommand — acceptable).
- **`oocockpit`**: after absorbing into `oopanel`, its embedded `ooagent-hud` subtree must move to the canonical `ooagent-hud`
  (reverse the embedding).
- **`oobuild-fleet`**: remove its embedded `oodeploy/` subtree — single source lives in `oodeploy`.
- **tools data family**: `oofilter`→merge into `ooawk`; `ootls`→merge into `oossl`.
- **`oostructureddiff`/`oosemantcdiff`/`ooschemadiff`/`ooastdiff`/`oogitdiff`**: collapse to one `oostructureddiff` host with
  format personas (ast/schema/semantic/git).

### 5.5 RFC/text amendments required (doc-law drift)

1. RFC 0012 L7 list says **`oofalse`** — almost certainly `oofalsify` (a tools↔agents name collision *inside the RFC itself*).
   Fix the RFC.
2. RFC L4 list vs `northstar.oot` L4 list disagree (`oosettings`+`oolock` vs `oowm`+`oocockpit`); implementation matches the RFC
   — update `northstar`.
3. Add `ooflash` to the L5 canonical list; decide `oochat`-vs-`oomail` canonical direction (code picked `oochat`; RFC picked
   `oomail` — pick one, prefer `oomail` as host name with `oochat` persona since "mail" is the superset domain).
4. Record `ooconsent→ooidentity`, `ooqueue→oodb-dist` decisions in the RFC mapping (implementation chose them; doc never did) —
   and kill the `oosched-cloud`/`oogateway` duplicate embeddings.
5. Declare `status` a meta-org repo in `northstar` (it's a real repo; doc says 4–5).
6. Reconcile core count (9 dirs vs doc claims of 10–11) and tools count (257 vs 258 incl. the github.io repo).
7. `oooda-engine` §4.1 advertises persona symlink applets — scrub the doc (no recipe found in Makefile, but `make build` text
   says it installs `bin/ooplanner`/`bin/ooarchitect` symlinks; §1.25 forbids them as files; install the `link-law` gate in all
   16 agents + all 18 cloud repos — currently absent there).

